# FHIR R4 Patient.mrn Element

In FHIR R4, there is **no element called `Patient.mrn`**.

Instead, Medical Record Numbers (MRNs) are represented using the **`Patient.identifier`** element, which is a repeating array of Identifier data types.

## Correct Usage

To represent an MRN in FHIR R4, you would structure it like this:

```json
{
  "resourceType": "Patient",
  "identifier": [
    {
      "type": {
        "coding": [
          {
            "system": "http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/v2-0203",
            "code": "MR"
          }
        ]
      },
      "system": "http://hospital.example.com/mrn",
      "value": "12345678"
    }
  ]
}
```

## Key Points

- **`identifier`** is used for all types of identifiers (MRN, SSN, etc.)
- The **`type`** field specifies that this is an MR (Medical Record) identifier
- The **`system`** indicates the assigning authority
- The **`value`** contains the actual MRN number

This flexible approach allows a single Patient resource to contain multiple identifiers from different systems.
